.TH NOSTR-HOMED-PROVISION-ENROLL 1 "2026-09-25" "nostr-homed 0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nostr-homed-provision-enroll \- generate a portable-home identity and write an account file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-homed-provision enroll
[\fB\-\-pubkey\fR \fIHEX\fR \fB\-\-secret\fR \fIHEX\fR]
[\fB\-\-relay\fR \fIwss://...\fR]...
[\fB\-\-blossom\fR \fIhttps://...\fR]...
[\fB\-\-d\-tag\fR \fISTR\fR]
[\fB\-\-out\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-seed\-drop\fR \fB\-\-uid\fR \fIUID\fR]
[\fB\-\-publish\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-redact\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates a fresh secp256k1 identity, derives a wrap_seed and home_key,
writes a 0600 account file, and optionally publishes the initial (gen 0)
kind-30078 pointer to the configured relays. If
.B \-\-pubkey
and
.B \-\-secret
are supplied, the existing identity is imported instead of generated.
.PP
The account file is the durable record of the portable-home identity: it is
the input to
.BR nostr-homed-provision-push (1),
.BR nostr-homed-provision-pull (1),
and
.BR nostr-homed-provision-verify (1),
and the material that the broker seed-drop path feeds to
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
and
.BR nostr-home-fuse (8).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-pubkey \fIHEX\fR
Use HEX as the account pubkey. Must be paired with
.BR \-\-secret .
.TP
.B \-\-secret \fIHEX\fR
Use HEX as the account nsec (raw 64-hex, no bech32 wrapper).
.TP
.B \-\-relay \fIwss://...\fR
Add a home relay. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-blossom \fIhttps://...\fR
Add a Blossom server. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-d\-tag \fISTR\fR
Override the pointer d-tag. Default:
.IR nostr-homed.home.v1:personal .
.TP
.B \-\-out\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Write \fB<pubkey8>.account.json\fR to DIR (0600). If omitted, the file goes
to stdout in a JSON block and no persistent artifact is left behind.
.TP
.B \-\-seed\-drop
Also write \fB/run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/home_seed\fR (mode 0400, owned
by the target uid). Requires
.B \-\-uid
and root.
.TP
.B \-\-uid \fIUID\fR
Target uid for the seed-drop.
.TP
.B \-\-publish
After enrolment, publish the empty gen-0 pointer to every
.BR \-\-relay .
Uses the same publish path as
.BR push .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print planned actions only. No file writes, no relay traffic.
.TP
.B \-\-redact
Replace secret fields with \(dqREDACTED\(dq in stdout output. Safe for
pasting into tickets.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <out-dir>/<pubkey8>.account.json
Account file (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/home_seed
Broker seed drop, when
.B \-\-seed\-drop
is used. Mode 0400; owned by the target uid.
.SH SECURITY
Runs OpenSSL secure heap; sets RLIMIT_CORE=0; wipes secret buffers before
exit. The account file mode is enforced at write time and re-checked before
any subsequent read. The seed drop is written atomically (temp + rename)
and never left with a wider mode.
.SH EXIT CODES
.RS
.TP 4
.B 0
Success.
.TP 4
.B 1
Malformed input (missing required option, invalid hex).
.TP 4
.B 2
Invalid combination (e.g.
.B \-\-pubkey
without
.BR \-\-secret ).
.TP 4
.B 5
File-system or permission error writing the account file.
.TP 4
.B 71
Publish failed (relay unreachable or refused). Only with
.BR \-\-publish .
.TP 4
.B 75
Crypto error during key derivation.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Fresh identity with two relays and two Blossom servers, initial pointer
published:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nostr-homed-provision enroll \\
    \-\-relay wss://relay.example \\
    \-\-relay wss://relay.backup \\
    \-\-blossom https://blossom.example \\
    \-\-blossom https://blossom.backup \\
    \-\-out\-dir ~/.config/nostr-homed \\
    \-\-publish
.fi
.RE
.PP
System-level provisioning that hands the seed to the broker session:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo nostr-homed-provision enroll \\
    \-\-relay wss://relay.example \\
    \-\-blossom https://blossom.example \\
    \-\-out\-dir /var/lib/nostr-auth/accounts \\
    \-\-seed\-drop \-\-uid 1001
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1),
.BR nostr-homed-provision-push (1),
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
